# When to update nearcrawl.mdc

`.cursor/rules/nearcrawl.mdc` is standing orders. `docs/architecture.md` and `docs/plans/` are the map. Update the rule only for durable policy. Do not refresh it on every code change.

## Update `nearcrawl.mdc` in the same change when

- You add or remove an app or shared package (one line only)
- You change how migrations, deploys, secrets, or required env work
- You add a convention every agent task must follow
- The same agent mistake happens more than once and the rule does not cover it

Keep the change small. Do not paste the route list, the article columns, or a directory tree into the rule.

## Do not update `nearcrawl.mdc` when

- You add a use case, a SQL file, a Drizzle column, or a repository method
- The detail already belongs in `docs/architecture.md` or a file under `docs/plans/`

## Also update the map

When you add or remove an app, package, or data store, update [docs/architecture.md](docs/architecture.md). That file owns the tree. The rule points at it.
